report='''# Phase 2C — feature reproducibility and deployment compatibility audit\n\n## Result: PHASE_2C_REQUIRES_EVIDENCE_EXTENSION\n\n### Scope and evidence reviewed\n\nThe live repository was audited, including `/assess`, its parser calls, feature engineers, sufficiency gate, scorer and the frozen Phase 2B.6 derivation. PRISM currently ingests bank statements, salary slips and utility bills. Its universal classifier runs BANK, SALARY and UTILITY extractors; no credit-card statement, loan-account statement or bureau-report parser exists. The actual assessment route uses PDF text extraction (pdfplumber/PyMuPDF) with OCR fallback for bank/utility documents and OCR/native text plus an LLM extractor for salary documents. A separate PDF/image acquisition class exists, but is not the parser path used by `/assess`.\n\n### Frozen Phase 2B.6 feature meanings\n\n1. `recent_delinquency_level`: raw `PAY_0`, September 2005; code first maps -2 and -1 to 0. Positive values represent delayed-month categories, capped at 9+. This is a credit repayment status, not bank overdraft.\n2. `months_with_delinquency`: count of positive recoded statuses across PAY_0, PAY_2, PAY_3, PAY_4, PAY_5 and PAY_6, corresponding to September through April 2005. Missing history cannot be called clean.\n3. `payment_to_statement_ratio`: sum of six PAY_AMT fields divided by the sum of positive-part BILL_AMT fields across the same six aligned months. A non-positive denominator yields unavailable, not zero. Negative payment inputs are invalid; negative statement amounts are clipped only in this denominator because the frozen code explicitly does so.\n4. `mean_statement_balance`: arithmetic mean of BILL_AMT1..6 over April-September 2005, retaining signed values. It is credit-card bill balance, not bank-account balance.\n\nThe full formula/source-column specification is in `phase2b6_feature_definitions.json`. UCI describes the delayed-month repayment scale and source dataset; the experiment code supplies the -2/-1 recode and exact aggregation.\n\n### Current PRISM trace and capability limits\n\n`bank PDF/text/OCR -> UniversalParser/BankExtractor -> date, narration, generic CR/DR amount, row closing_balance -> BankFeatureEngineer -> scorer` is the current bank path. `credit_debit_ratio` is total CR / total DR (missing when denominator is zero). `cashflow_cv` is sample standard deviation of monthly net transaction sums divided by their mean (requires at least two months and nonzero mean). `min_balance_l3m` is the minimum extracted bank transaction closing balance from the latest transaction date minus three months; scorer maps this to `min_balance`.\n\n`salary PDF/OCR/native text -> SalaryParser/LLM extraction -> gross_salary/net_salary -> SalaryFeatureEngineer -> scorer` yields `net_to_gross_ratio = net/gross`, missing for absent values or gross <=0. A payroll amount is not a repayment.\n\n`utility PDF/text/OCR -> UniversalParser/UtilityExtractor -> bill amount, due date, consumer number, keyword payment marker -> UtilityFeatureEngineer -> scorer` is a separate utility signal. The utility extractor does not currently extract `missed_payments` or `payment_date`; a single bill amount cannot produce its amount-CV component. Utility payment behavior is not credit delinquency.\n\nThe scorer requires all five existing features, >=6 transactions, >=90 elapsed bank-history days, >=3 utility observations, quality >=0.60, and documents no older than 180 days. This does not establish six complete calendar months, aligned card statements, or continuity. It also requires bank, salary and utility evidence; those requirements are existing behavior and were not changed.\n\nThe route records coarse source names, counts, dates and extraction quality, but not stable per-feature document/page/raw-field lineage. Upload files are deleted after assessment. This is inadequate provenance for the proposed credit-account features.\n\n### Compatibility matrix\n\n| Feature | Current parser compatibility | Result | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| recent_delinquency_level | No card/loan status or bureau DPD | REPRODUCIBLE_WITH_NEW_DOCUMENT_TYPE | Requires explicit account-level repayment status/months past due. |\n| months_with_delinquency | No monthly creditor status history | REPRODUCIBLE_WITH_NEW_DOCUMENT_TYPE | Requires six ordered credit-account status months. |\n| payment_to_statement_ratio | Generic bank debits and no card billed balance | REPRODUCIBLE_WITH_NEW_DOCUMENT_TYPE | Requires six same-account, month-aligned statement/payment pairs. |\n| mean_statement_balance | Bank transaction closing balance only | REPRODUCIBLE_WITH_NEW_DOCUMENT_TYPE | Requires six credit-card billed statement balances. |\n\nNo feature is directly reproducible today. A generic bank debit is not automatically a card payment; bank account balance, utility delay and cash-flow volatility are not delinquency or card statement balance. The four features remain relevant to a credit behavior model, so Architecture B is more defensible than treating UCI as conceptually unrelated.\n\n### Experimental contract and fail-closed behavior\n\nA non-production Feature Schema v2 contract was added. It requires six consecutive calendar months before an exclusive cutoff, account/product identity, document and page/record identifiers, raw-to-normalized field mapping, extraction method and confidence. It distinguishes `MISSING_REQUIRED_EVIDENCE` from explicitly verified `NOT_APPLICABLE`; the latter has no score mapping. Missing, incomplete or future evidence never becomes zero. A zero ratio numerator with a positive denominator yields zero; a zero denominator yields `INSUFFICIENT_DENOMINATOR`; negative payments are invalid; signed statement balances are preserved for the mean and clipped only in the frozen ratio denominator.\n\nThe contract validates prospective normalized evidence only. It is not an OCR parser, current PRISM adapter, endpoint integration or production feature implementation. No direct compatibility fixture exists because the current parser cannot provide these semantics. Test fixtures validate only the proposed contract and do not claim parser support.\n\n### Minimum extension and decision\n\nAdd a typed `CreditAccountMonthlyHistory` evidence source (or a parser for six consecutive credit-card statements) with account identifier/product type, statement month, billed balance, corresponding payment amount, explicit repayment status/months past due, and field-level provenance. If statements do not provide status, add product-specific bureau repayment history or lender account history. Bureau history alone should not be presumed to contain monthly statement balances and payments. Structured issuer/bureau data is preferable to OCR where available. Obtain purpose-specific user consent before accessing new credit/bureau evidence.\n\nNo UCI target fitting, retraining, parser integration, route change, frontend change, or production promotion occurred. Phase 2B.6 remains `PHASE_2B6_INCONCLUSIVE`; its files were hash-checked unchanged. Production artifact hashes were also checked against the captured pre-audit snapshot.\n\n### Architecture decision\n\n`B — Extend PRISM evidence`\n\n### Next engineering action\n\nSpecify and review the minimum six-month credit-account evidence contract and consent flow before implementing a non-production parser. Do not begin that work automatically.\n'''
report += '''\n\n## Source references\n\n- [UCI Default of Credit Card Clients documentation](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/350/defaultofcreditcardclients) describes the target and repayment-status scale.\n- Exact recoding and aggregation semantics above were additionally verified against the frozen local experiment source: `backend/phase2/real_evidence/run_phase2b5r.py` and `backend/phase2/real_evidence/run_phase2b6.py`.\n- Current ingestion claims were verified against `backend/route/assessment_routes.py`, `backend/ingestion/universal_pipeline.py`, `backend/features/*.py`, and `backend/scoring/risk_scorer.py`.\n'''
(OUT/'semantic_mapping_report.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
